        "code": "from soar.platform.runtime import log_event, services\n\nimport json\n\nrows = db.query(\n    \"SELECT execution_id, node_id, status, attempt, duration_ms \"\n    \"FROM execution_step WHERE id = %s\", [step_id], org_id,\n)\nif not rows:\n    return\n\ntry:\n    services()[\"redis\"].publish(\"events:execution\", json.dumps({\n        \"execution_id\": rows[0][\"execution_id\"],\n        \"step_id\": step_id,\n        \"node_id\": rows[0][\"node_id\"],\n        \"status\": rows[0][\"status\"],\n        \"attempt\": rows[0][\"attempt\"],\n    }))\nexcept Exception:\n    log_event(\"warning\", \"execution_event_publish_failed\", {\"step_id\": step_id})",
        "doc": "Tell the live execution console that a step changed.\n\nBest effort, and deliberately so: a failed notification must never fail the\nstep that succeeded. The console falls back to polling, which is slower and\ncorrect rather than faster and wrong.",
